# A hub: one building with many individuals linked to it, to see the limits on drawing individuals (issue #209). The file has 135
# individuals, more than the 30 that are drawn by themselves, so on opening the graph shows only the four classes. Then:
#   - open the Individuals tab (the toolbar says "Individuals (135)"): the individuals are listed by type (filter them by label or name above), each type a closed row,
#     the biggest first: Sensor (120), Room (12), Floor (2), Building (1)
#   - press the button on the Sensor row, "Show 50 (0 displayed/120 total)": 50 sensors are drawn, beside the classes, and it reads
#     "Show 50 more (50 displayed/120 total)" for the next 50, then "Show 20 more (100 displayed/120 total)", then "All 120 displayed"
#   - open a type (its arrow) to list its individuals: each row has its own button, "Show 1 (0 displayed/1 total)", that draws that
#     individual alone, and reads "All 1 displayed" once it is drawn, however it was drawn (the sensors above, for one); drawn rows
#     are marked with an orange dot and background
#   - open Building and choose Head office (click its name): its detail has "Show 50 neighbours (0 displayed/122 total)" for its
#     two floors and 120 sensors, 50 at a time: "Show 50 more neighbours (50 displayed/122 total)", "Show 22 more neighbours (100 displayed/122 total)", then
#     "All 122 neighbours displayed"
#   - "Reset view" in the graph also clears the individuals; "Clear individuals" in the tab does too
#   - each sensor's "reading" is in its tooltip
#   - the same file with more than 300 individuals asked for would show the first 300 with a warning
@prefix : <http://example.org/examples/individuals-hub#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

<http://example.org/examples/individuals-hub> a owl:Ontology ; rdfs:label "Individuals, a hub" .

:Building a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Building" .
:Floor a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Floor" .
:Room a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Room" .
:Sensor a owl:Class ; rdfs:label "Sensor" .
:partOf a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "part of" .
:installedIn a owl:ObjectProperty ; rdfs:label "installed in" ; rdfs:domain :Sensor ; rdfs:range :Building .
:reading a owl:DatatypeProperty ; rdfs:domain :Sensor ; rdfs:range xsd:decimal .

:hq a :Building ; rdfs:label "Head office" .
:floor1 a :Floor ; rdfs:label "Floor 1" ; :partOf :hq .
:floor2 a :Floor ; rdfs:label "Floor 2" ; :partOf :hq .
:room1 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 1" ; :partOf :floor1 .
:room2 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 2" ; :partOf :floor1 .
:room3 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 3" ; :partOf :floor1 .
:room4 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 4" ; :partOf :floor1 .
:room5 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 5" ; :partOf :floor1 .
:room6 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 6" ; :partOf :floor1 .
:room7 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 7" ; :partOf :floor2 .
:room8 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 8" ; :partOf :floor2 .
:room9 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 9" ; :partOf :floor2 .
:room10 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 10" ; :partOf :floor2 .
:room11 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 11" ; :partOf :floor2 .
:room12 a :Room ; rdfs:label "Room 12" ; :partOf :floor2 .
:sensor001 a :Sensor ; rdfs:label "Sensor 001" ; :installedIn :hq ; :reading 16.0 .
:sensor002 a :Sensor ; rdfs:label "Sensor 002" ; :installedIn :hq ; :reading 17.0 .
:sensor003 a :Sensor ; rdfs:label "Sensor 003" ; :installedIn :hq ; :reading 18.0 .
